From: PupJune2 <PupJune2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: CromIKO Theme

Restyle the Android UI around the CromIKO logo colors:
- regenerate the primary, secondary and neutral tonal palettes from the
  logo accent (#5C7CFC) and charcoal (#1E2024); the charcoal is used as
  neutral_10 and as the dark surface container color
- re-tint the GM3 light/dark surfaces to match
- keep the brand palette on Android 12+ instead of wallpaper-based
  dynamic colors (a theme color chosen in the NTP customization still
  applies)
- use the brand colors for the splash screen background on Android 12+

Tertiary (green) and error colors are unchanged so that success and
error states keep their meaning.

License: GPL-3.0-only - https://spdx.org/licenses/GPL-3.0-only.html
